              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to float away, then the Telugu for to be swept away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పైలటు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పైలటు — pailaṭu — \"a pilot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "విమానం దిగే ముందు పైలటు మాతో మాట్లాడాడు. vimānaṁ digē mundu pailaṭu mātō māṭlāḍāḍu. Before the plane landed, the pilot spoke to us."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Like other English loans it takes -ఉ: పైలటు (pailaṭu). A woman pilot is also పైలటు (pailaṭu)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పైలటు (pailaṭu) is a loan from English pilot, with the Telugu final -ఉ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
