        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అంతర్జాతీయ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అంతర్జాతీయ — antarjātīya — \"international\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మా నగరంలో కొత్త అంతర్జాతీయ విమానాశ్రయం ఉంది. mā nagaraṁlō kotta antarjātīya vimānāśrayaṁ undi. There is a new international airport in our city."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An adjective that stands before its noun and does not change: అంతర్జాతీయ (antarjātīya) విమానం, an international flight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అంతర్జాతీయ (antarjātīya) is a learned word built from Sanskrit: antar, \"between\", jāti, \"birth, a people, a nation\", and the adjective ending -īya (Monier-Williams): between the nations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
