          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాగనంపు — sāganampu — \"to see off\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మేము అత్తను విమానాశ్రయంలో సాగనంపాం. mēmu attanu vimānāśrayaṁlō sāganampāṁ. We saw our aunt off at the airport."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): సాగనంపాను, sāganampānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాగను, to go on, + అంపు, to send: to send someone on their way. Telugu families often go to the station to see a guest off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాగనంపు (sāganampu) is native Dravidian: సాగను, from సాగు, \"to go on, to proceed\" (DEDR 2430), and అంపు, \"to send\" (DEDR 329)."
            }
          ]
        },
